  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "parseResources",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/DnsLayer.cpp",
    "description": "DnsLayer::parseResources() trusts the DNS header's resource counts and constructs a DnsQuery/DnsResource at offsetInPacket before validating that the offset is within m_DataLen; its only bounds check occurs after the constructor and getSize() have already parsed the record. Consequently IDnsResource's constructor passes getRawData() to IDnsResource::decodeName(), which performs the observed one-byte heap out-of-bounds read at the end of the captured packet. The parser must validate that a resource begins in-bounds (and that its fixed fields fit) before constructing/parsing it, then reject truncated resource lists.",
    "conditions": "A captured packet must be parsed as UDP DNS (source or destination port 53/5353/5355 and at least a DNS header), while the attacker-controlled DNS count fields claim more query/resource records than are actually present. In this PoV the pcap reader supplies the crafted packet to Packet parsing; the DNS header advertises 129 questions and 159 answers (288 total, below the existing 300-record cutoff), but the DNS payload is truncated after the header/minimal bytes. parseResources advances through the available bytes and then attempts to construct another query at the packet boundary, causing decodeName to read beyond the heap allocation."
  },
